"README.md (1194 bytes)\n     1→# greet-pkg\n     2→\n     3→A minimal Node.js package that exports a simple greeting function.\n     4→\n     5→## Install\n     6→\n     7→```bash\n     8→npm install greet-pkg\n     9→```\n    10→\n    11→For a reproducible install from the lockfile:\n    12→\n    13→```bash\n    14→npm ci\n    15→```\n    16→\n    17→## Usage\n    18→\n    19→```js\n    20→const { greet } = require(\"./index\");\n    21→\n    22→greet();        // \"Hello, world!\"\n    23→greet(\"Ada\");   // \"Hello, Ada!\"\n    24→```\n    25→\n    26→## API\n    27→\n    28→### `greet(name?)`\n    29→\n    30→Returns the string `Hello, <name>!`. Defaults to `\"world\"` when `name` is omitted.\n    31→\n    32→## Integrity and reproducibility\n    33→\n    34→- Exact SHA-256 hashes of the source and manifest files (`index.js`, `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `README.md`) are recorded in `checksums.txt` (standard `sha256sum` format).\n    35→- Verify the inputs have not changed:\n    36→\n    37→  ```bash\n    38→  sha256sum -c checksums.txt\n    39→  ```\n    40→\n    41→- Regenerate `checksums.txt` after an intentional change:\n    42→\n    43→  ```bash\n    44→  npm run hash\n    45→  ```\n    46→\n    47→- Dependencies: none — the lockfile currently pins only the root package. Any dependency added in the future must be declared in `package.json` with an exact pinned version (no `^` or `~` ranges); `npm install --package-lock-only` then pins the full resolved graph in `package-lock.json`, including every transitive version and its integrity hash.\n    48→\n    49→## License\n    50→\n    51→MIT\n    52→"